 ## Overview
-VoxNeRF is a neural rendering method that integrates explicit scene geometry priors (mesh, point cloud, or depth map) with implicit radiance field representation to improve sampling efficiency and reconstruction accuracy [S1]. It addresses the ill-posed nature of recovering 3D geometry from 2D images by using a Sparse Voxel Octree (SVO) to model geometric uncertainty, which guides a hybrid sampling strategy [S1]. Unlike standard NeRF methods that sample uniformly or via stratified noise, VoxNeRF concentrates samples near the estimated surface while maintaining coverage of free space, reducing computational waste in empty regions [S1].
+VoxNeRF is a neural rendering method that integrates explicit scene geometry priors (mesh, point cloud, or depth map) with an implicit radiance field representation to improve sampling efficiency and reconstruction accuracy [S1]. It addresses the ill-posed nature of recovering 3D geometry from 2D images by using a Sparse Voxel Octree (SVO) to model geometric uncertainty, which guides a hybrid sampling strategy [S1]. Unlike standard NeRF methods that sample uniformly or via stratified noise, VoxNeRF concentrates samples near the estimated surface while maintaining coverage of free space, reducing computational waste in empty regions [S1].
 
